{"ts": "2026-11-27T00:42:36.332714Z", "run_id": "r-20261127T0036Z-041d", "unit": "openspec:add-web-tool-trust", "seq": 12, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "Verified in ReviewSections.tsx that Discover tools builds its body from discoverSettings(storedTools(approved)) and initialDraft of the approved tools, in trust.ts that a retry flag equal to the adapter default is not carried and that valueChangeLines only emits lines for fields that differ, in review.ts that an empty entry is dropped, and in the e2e file that the asserted body and item texts match. The DataTable wrapper has overflow-x auto, so the wider table keeps the layout assertion. The browser test was not run in a gate, but every assertion follows from the code.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "C-c8329b48", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.887099, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "f09aaacb19818352077cbf3f0acda12200fd3dfb3152b1efcfd48eec1daa7822", "checked": [{"ref": "web/src/tools/ReviewSections.tsx:182", "quote": "const settings = discoverSettings(storedTools(approved));", "claim": "Discover tools posts the approved surface's trust and carried values, which are all defaults in this scenario."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/trust.ts:124", "quote": "stored.unsafe_to_retry !== defaultRetry(adapter, next.effect)", "claim": "A stored unsafe_to_retry equal to the MCP default true is not carried, so no retry member reaches the body."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/review.ts:544", "quote": "if (Object.keys(entry).length > 0) tools[key] = entry;", "claim": "log_note and old_tool with Proposed effect and default trust give empty entries and are left out of the body."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/trust.ts:343", "quote": "if (old.effect !== next.effect) lines.push(`Effect: ${old.effect} → ${next.effect}`);", "claim": "Value lines are added only for fields that differ, so find_vendor (hints only) gets none and log_note gets an Effect line under its unchanged item text."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/ReviewSections.tsx:114", "quote": "const cv = withValueLines(", "claim": "The Changes list is changesView with value lines appended, keeping each item's text."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m7_tool_review.py:408", "quote": "assert posts[0][\"body\"] == {\"tools\": {\"find_vendor\": {\"effect\": \"read\"}}}", "claim": "The frozen test pins the Discover tools body that the code builds."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:6", "quote": "overflow-x: auto;", "claim": "The DataTable wrapper scrolls horizontally, so the two added columns do not widen the page for the layout assertion."}]}
